    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0301" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/334</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Queenstown</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-02-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received February 13, 1.25 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British tanker <hi rendition="#italic">Saxonian</hi> left Newport News, January
                    25 for Queenstown, crew 38, three Americans, no gun, no wireless. Shelled 5.15
                    p.m., February 7, 280 miles southwest Fastnet. No attempt escape. When 32 shells
                    failed, submarine torpedoed <hi rendition="#italic">Saxonian</hi> about <pb
                        facs="0302" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/> 6 p.m., sinking her. Then approached
                    crew in two open boats and asked vessel’s nationality, no offer assistance.
                    Weather: heavy swells, fresh southeast wind, darkness. One boat picked up after
                    68 hours, other also, time unknown. When other boat’s crew lands to-morrow
                    morning can say if any Americans lost. One saved in crew already landed. This
                    telegram sent Ambassador, Consul General.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
